$DATUM N-(2-(Benzo[d][1,3]dioxol-5-yl)ethyl)-2-(2-bromophenyl)-2-hydroxyacetamide
(10) To a solution of 3,4-methylenedioxyphenethylamine hydrochloride (8)
(590 mg, 2.9 mmol), 2-bromomandelic acid (9) (750 mg, 3.2 mmol), HOBt
hydrate (495 mg, 3.2 mmol) and N,N-diisopropylethylamine (0.6 mL, 3.5
mmol) in anhydrous DMF (5 mL) was added EDC (620 mg, 3.2 mmol) under
argon. The resulting mixture was stirred at room temperature for 16 h and
then quenched by the addition of 1 M HCl(aq). The aqueous layer was
extracted with EtOAc (2 × 50 mL). After neutralization with saturated
aqueous NaHCO3, the combined organic extracts were washed with brine,
dried over anhydrous MgSO4, filtered and concentrated. The residue was
purified by column chromatography on silica gel (EtOAc/hexane, 40:60 to
50:50), 10 (980 mg, 88%) as a colorless oil. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 500 MHz) 7.52
(1 H, d, J = 8.0 Hz), 7.40 (1 H, d, J = 7.5 Hz), 7.34 (1 H, t, J = 8.0
Hz), 7.19 (1 H, t, J = 7.5 Hz), 6.65 (1 H, d, J = 8.0 Hz), 6.50 (1 H, d,
J = 1.7 Hz), 6.43 (1 H, dd, J = 8.0, 1.7 Hz), 6.09 (1 H, br, NH), 5.93 (2
H, s), 5.42 (1 H, d, J = 4.6 Hz), 4.18 (1 H, d, J = 4.6 Hz, OH),
3.59-3.53 (1 H, m), 3.46-3.40 (1 H, m), 2.72-2.60 (2 H, m); 13C NMR
(CDCl3, 125 MHz) 171.4, 147.7, 146.1, 139.0, 132.8, 131.9, 129.8, 128.5,
128.1, 122.7, 121.5, 108.9, 108.3, 100.8, 72.0, 40.9, 35.0; HRMS
(DART-TOF) m/z calculated for C17H17BrNO4 [M + H]+: 378.0341; found:
378.0322.
